FriendlyElec SOM-RK3399 support targets the board's standard lab layout:
SD card firmware plus a full FreeBSD system image written to eMMC.

============================================================

What is a SOM-RK3399?
---------------------

The FriendlyElec SOM-RK3399 is an RK3399 based ARM64 compute module.
This board definition is intended for the SOM-RK3399 v2 setup with
FreeBSD booted by U-Boot via EFI.

============================================================

Boot model
----------

This board does not build a single self-contained SD system image.
Instead:

1. The SD card carries Rockchip firmware only:
   * idbloader.img at sector 64
   * u-boot.itb at sector 16384

2. The Crochet output image is the FreeBSD eMMC system image:
   * FAT ESP containing BOOTAA64.EFI and rk3399-som-rk3399.dtb
   * UFS root partition containing the kernel and world

U-Boot is expected to load BOOTAA64.EFI and
rk3399-som-rk3399.dtb from the eMMC ESP and then execute bootefi.

============================================================

Prerequisites
-------------

1. /usr/src must contain:
   * sys/arm64/conf/SOM_RK3399
   * sys/contrib/device-tree/src/arm64/rockchip/rk3399-som-rk3399.dts
   * a Rockchip DTB module Makefile that lists rk3399-som-rk3399.dts

2. If /usr/src is missing the DTS, Crochet will migrate it from:
   /linux/oh-my-bsdlab/external/freebsd-src

3. The Rockchip firmware artifacts must exist. By default Crochet looks for:
   * /linux/oh-my-bsdlab/external/som-rk3399/u-boot/idbloader.img
   * /linux/oh-my-bsdlab/external/som-rk3399/u-boot/u-boot.itb

You can override those paths with:
   * SOM_RK3399_FIRMWARE_ROOT
   * SOM_RK3399_IDBLOADER
   * SOM_RK3399_UBOOT_ITB

============================================================

How to build
------------

Create a config file whose first line is:

    board_setup SOM-RK3399

Then run:

    sudo /bin/sh crochet.sh -c <config file>

The result is a FreeBSD system image for eMMC. Write the firmware to SD
using your existing SOM-RK3399 U-Boot workflow, then write the Crochet
image to eMMC.
